## Effort Estimate

**Recommended Model Tier:** Standard *(explicitly specified by the requester)*
**Reasoning:** The change is a small, well-bounded merge function with concrete numeric thresholds (50m / 10min) and no architectural or cross-module design decisions — too much domain-logic judgment (boundary handling, which record's fields win on merge) for Economy, but no design-space exploration warranting Premium.

---

## User Story

**As a** Fernglen product owner
**I want to** merge two sighting records into one when they report the same species within 50 meters and 10 minutes of each other
**So that** duplicate volunteer submissions stop double-counting a single observation

---

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Given two sighting records of the same species reported within 50 meters and within 10 minutes of each other, `dedupe_nearby_sightings()` merges them into a single sighting record.
- [ ] Given two sighting records of the same species reported more than 50 meters apart, `dedupe_nearby_sightings()` does not merge them (both records are preserved).
- [ ] Given two sighting records of the same species reported more than 10 minutes apart, `dedupe_nearby_sightings()` does not merge them (both records are preserved).
- [ ] Given two sighting records of different species (regardless of distance/time), `dedupe_nearby_sightings()` does not merge them.
- [ ] Boundary values (exactly 50 meters, exactly 10 minutes) are handled by an explicit, documented inclusive/exclusive rule and covered by a dedicated test case (see Technical Notes — merge-semantics is otherwise unspecified by the request).

---

